# AgentsDocContract.registry -- the document-contract guard's registry.
# One row per registered document extension, four TAB-separated columns.
#   kind      the validator kind of a document with this extension (routine, epic, ...)
#   extension the file-name ending that selects the row, with its leading dot (.routine.md), or a name pattern
#             holding `*`, matched on the file's own name (epic-blueprint-*.md): the vault's kinds are the type
#             word that opens the name, since a vault holds many file types and the extension stays the file's own
#   state     refusing | reporting | absent
#               refusing   a refusing fault the write introduces refuses the write
#               reporting  the fault is said and the write goes on
#               absent     the type is declared and its contract is not written yet: allow
#   contract  the kind's contract file, a bare name under magic-team/contracts, or - for absent
# An extension not named here is not a document type: the guard's default allows the write and
# decides nothing.
#
# Slice 1: the routine kind is registered, refusing.
routine	.routine.md	refusing	routine.contract.format.md
# Slice 2 (S12.30): the kinds with an extension of their own are declared, absent: the guard allows and decides nothing
# until each contract is written and its row turns reporting, then refusing. A kind named by a prefix (plan-, sprint-)
# waits for the registry to take a pattern.
vault-item.epic-blueprint	epic-blueprint-*.md	reporting	vault-item.epic-blueprint.contract.format.md
vault-item.investigation-report	investigation-*.md	reporting	vault-item.investigation-report.contract.format.md
vault-item.decision-record	adr-*.md	reporting	vault-item.decision-record.contract.format.md
vault-item.verbatim-record	verbatim-record-*.md	reporting	vault-item.verbatim-record.contract.format.md
planning	planning-*.md	absent	-
tracking	tracking-*.md	absent	-
magic	MAGIC.md	absent	-
